# ==============================================================================
# 🛑 Evidence safety — deny by default
# ==============================================================================
#
# data_store/ holds real forensic evidence. This file denies everything and
# re-includes only the directory skeleton and documentation.
#
# It used to be an extension blocklist. A blocklist fails silently on any format
# nobody thought to add, and that had already happened: VMware exports
# (.vmdk, -flat.vmdk, .vmx, .ovf, .ova, .vmsd, .vmxf) were fully committable,
# because VM support was added to the pipeline without updating the list —
# and data_store/raw/VM_files/ is the documented place to put them.
#
# Deny-by-default means the next format nobody thought of is covered too.
#
# STRUCTURE. Every re-include below is ANCHORED to an exact path, including the
# skeleton DIRECTORIES: a directory that is ignored and has no negation inside
# is pruned — git never descends into it. The old `!*/` form re-enabled descent
# into EVERY directory, so `git status` walked the entire evidence tree
# (terabytes, tens of seconds) on each run. It also means an evidence dir can
# never smuggle a file in via a name-based re-include: nothing inside a corpus
# directory is even looked at. Adding a new skeleton file = add its directory
# chain and the file here, tracked and reviewed like any other change.
#
# This is a safety net, not a guarantee. Check `git status` before committing.

# Ignore everything under data_store/ ...
*

# ... and re-include ONLY the exact skeleton, directory chains first.
#
# This file only (anchored) — NOT a bare `!.gitignore`, which un-ignores every
# nested .gitignore in the evidence (imaged filesystems carry hundreds). The
# same goes for `!.gitkeep` / `!README.md`: only the exact skeleton paths are
# re-included, never names.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md

!/dependencies/
!/dependencies/evtxecmd/
!/dependencies/evtxecmd/.gitkeep
!/dependencies/evtxecmd/README.md
# NOTE: /dependencies/hayabusa/ (fetched tool cache, embeds a git repo under
# rules/) needs no special rule any more — like every other unlisted directory
# it is ignored and pruned outright.

!/docker_images/
!/docker_images/.gitkeep

!/processed/
!/processed/csv/
!/processed/csv/.gitkeep
!/processed/json/
!/processed/json/.gitkeep
!/processed/linux_logs/
!/processed/linux_logs/.gitkeep
!/processed/log2timeline/
!/processed/log2timeline/.gitkeep
!/processed/software_logs/
!/processed/software_logs/.gitkeep
!/processed/velociraptor/
!/processed/velociraptor/README.md
!/processed/windows_logs/
!/processed/windows_logs/hostname1/
!/processed/windows_logs/hostname1/.gitkeep
!/processed/windows_logs/hostname2/
!/processed/windows_logs/hostname2/.gitkeep
!/processed/windows_logs/hostname3/
!/processed/windows_logs/hostname3/.gitkeep
!/processed/zeek/
!/processed/zeek/.gitkeep
!/processed/zimmerman/
!/processed/zimmerman/.gitkeep

!/raw/
!/raw/VM_files/
!/raw/VM_files/.gitkeep
!/raw/disk_images/
!/raw/disk_images/.gitkeep
!/raw/memory/
!/raw/memory/.gitkeep
!/raw/mobile/
!/raw/mobile/.gitkeep
!/raw/other_raw_data/
!/raw/other_raw_data/.gitkeep
!/raw/other_raw_data/documents/
!/raw/other_raw_data/documents/.gitkeep
!/raw/other_raw_data/host_extractions/
!/raw/other_raw_data/host_extractions/.gitkeep
!/raw/other_raw_data/WinEvt/
!/raw/other_raw_data/WinEvt/.gitkeep
!/raw/other_raw_data/sql/
!/raw/other_raw_data/sql/.gitkeep
!/raw/pcaps/
!/raw/pcaps/.gitkeep
